{
 "comment": "UPI handles and joins: payments of Wages from Bank A, and one receipt. One handle joins two names: h01 to h03 (ALPHA.T, h03 in lower case), h04 and h05 (BETA_S.9: letters, an underscore, a full stop, a digit), h06 and h07 (70412-2, with its one suffix of a hyphen and digits), h24 and h25 (NU.S, the @ being the last character of h24's narration), h26 and h27 (a suffix in Devanagari digits). h08's handle is 70412, another payee than 70412-2; h28's is XI-12, another than the one in Devanagari digits. No handle is read where the text before the @ holds a space (h10, h11), a suffix of a letter (h12, h13), two suffixes (h14, h15), an ampersand (h16, h17), nothing (h18, h19), a suffix and nothing before it (h41, h42), a letter outside A to Z (h22, h23), a Devanagari digit (h43, h44), or where the @ is the full-width one (h20, h21): each pair shares that text under two names and stays two payees. Second UPI layout, joined to a payment in the first layout by the handle its fourth field prints: h30 with h31 (the text after the @ dropped), h32 with h33 (the spaces inside the field removed), h36 with h37 (an empty bank field), h39 with h40 (cut at the first of two @). h34's fourth field has no closing slash, so no handle is read and h35 is another payee; h38's field starts with @, so no handle is read either. h50 and h51 are one name on two handles: one payee, keyed by the smaller handle (ABE.9, not ZED.1). h52 to h56 chain three names over two handles and an IMPS payment: one payee, three names, channels IMPS and UPI. h60 (PSI ONE, PSI.A) and h61 (PSI TWO, PSI.B) stay two payees: h62, which prints PSI ONE with PSI.B, is a receipt and joins nothing. Thirty-six payees, no finding.",
